spans.s:
sughoṣa,
(1) (m.) a kind of musical instrument, = the commoner ˚ṣaka, q.v. (cf. AMg. sughosā, f., acc. to Ratnach. a certain bell, ghaṇṭā): ˚ṣaṃ (acc.) Mv 〔ii.159.5〕; ˚ṣaiii.70.15; v.l. in 〔i.227.17〕 and 〔iii.407.19〕; all prose;
(2) n. of a former Buddha: LV 〔5.12〕; and acc. to Senartʼs em. Mv 〔i.137.1〕, see Sughoṣasamabuddhi.
